WS Grand Junction CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.\n\n* WHERE...Northeastern Montezuma County in southwestern Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 145 PM MDT Friday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 150 AM MDT, Gauge reports indicated heavy rain due to\nthunderstorms. Minor flooding is ongoing or expected to begin\nshortly in the advisory area.\n- This includes the following streams and drainages...\nDolores River and Lost Canyon Creek.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nDolores.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-23T13:45:00-06:00","severity":"Minor","areaDesc":"Montezuma, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.2fdf726d0fb13c0b88fc6dcb10d8286a91efdb38.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.2fdf726d0fb13c0b88fc6dcb10d8286a91efdb38.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued October 23 at 12:01AM MDT until October 23 at 12:00PM MDT by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.\n\n* WHERE...Southern Montezuma County in southwestern Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until noon MDT Friday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of rivers, creeks, streams, and other low-lying\nand flood-prone locations is imminent or occurring. Streams\ncontinue to rise due to excess runoff from earlier rainfall.\nLow-water crossings are inundated with water and may not be\npassable.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 1201 AM MDT, Doppler radar and gauges indicated heavy rain.\nFlooding is ongoing or expected to begin shortly in the warned\narea.\n- This includes the following streams and drainages...\nEast Mancos River, West Mancos River,  Middle Mancos River, Ute\nCanyon, West Fork Mud Creek, Lewis Creek, Lost Canyon Creek, East\nCanyon, and Mancos River.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nMancos and Mesa Verde Natl Park.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-23T12:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Montezuma, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e4b61b6755353b5697b2bae251afeae25e693ad6.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e4b61b6755353b5697b2bae251afeae25e693ad6.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued October 22 at 9:50PM MDT until October 24 at 12:00AM MDT by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...Portions of southwest Colorado, including the following\nareas, Animas River Basin, Four Corners/Upper Dolores River, San\nJuan River Basin and Southwest San Juan Mountains and Utah,\nincluding the following areas, Arches/Grand Flat,\nCanyonlands/Natural Bridges, La Sal and Abajo Mountains and\nSoutheast Utah.\n\n* WHEN...Through Friday evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, recent burn scars and other low-lying and\nflood-prone locations. Low-water crossings may be flooded. Storm\ndrains and ditches may become clogged with debris.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Flooding is imminent or ongoing with additional rounds of showers\nand thunderstorms expected through Friday afternoon. Rivers and\ncreeks may still experience high waters even after rainfall has\nended.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-24T00:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Uncompahgre Plateau/Dallas Divide; Northwestern San Juan Mountains; Southwest San Juan Mountains; Paradox Valley/Lower Dolores River; Four Corners/Upper Dolores River; Animas River Basin; San Juan River Basin; Southeast Utah; Arches/Grand Flat; La Sal and Abajo Mountains; Canyonlands/Natural Bridges","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e0dbcacb680ad71bb79dff518cb60ff22ebdb688.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e0dbcacb680ad71bb79dff518cb60ff22ebdb688.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warn